## Column set — a decision, not the fallback

The brief offered a 9-column shape *"if none specifies a CSV shape exactly."* One does: `compliance-source-hunter` §3.3 fixes **exactly 20 columns in order**, and `shared/schemas/README.md` points at it. The fallback was conditional, so I used the real contract. Same doctrine names Belgium as the country that *"produced no register at all"* — it now has one.

## L-01 — `00-official-sources/legal-basis-register.csv`

**63 rows × 20 columns.** Domains: income_tax 17 · social_security 13 · statutory_reporting 10 · benefits_in_kind 8 · live_legal_change 3 · labour_code 3 · indexation 2 · payslip_statute 2 · termination 2 · collective_agreements 1 · leave 1 · deductions_garnishments 1. Tier A.1 33 / A.2 27 / A.3 1 / B 2.

Every item you named is in, plus: the three allowance figures are **three separate rows** so the two wrong ones are rejectable by id (`BE-PIT-006` = 11,180, `status=superseded`, `effective_from` = "never in force"); the 13.92 factor is deliberately **tier B** with "MERCANS CONVENTION, NOT A STATUTORY FIGURE" in its name — a tier-B row carrying a number is exactly the flag it should raise on every P2.

**`consumed_by` was measured, not guessed.** All eight artifacts were dumped to text and each row carries regex probes matched against them: **384 tokens over 28 units** (CCG 194, WTC 46, RSPEC 32, SKILL 29, SCOPE 28, PSL 24, DD 18, SIR 13).

I then audited the measurement rather than trusting it, and **nine false-positive consumers came out**: `6/7` was matching `96/71/EC` (Posting of Workers Directive), bare `92%` was matching `24.92%`, `498` was matching Moldova's ISO currency code, `509` was matching reorganisation code lists `501…512`, and `one-fifth` was matching the one-fifth *time credit*, not the Article 23 cap.

**Two rows measure empty, and that is the finding:** the Law of 15 July 2026 and coefficient 2.3356 are cited in **no delivered artifact** (zero hits for seven distinct search terms). 11,550 and 11,180 appear only in `SKILL.md` — so `ALLOWANCE_INVESTIGATION.md` §3.2's instruction that the CCG state the 11,170-withholding / 11,550-assessment split **never landed in the CCG**. Carried at §1I.3, declared not fixed — that's an artifact content change, outside this pass.

## L-04 — ledger reframing

§0 now says the register **is** the checklist going forward and a missing consumer line is a **defect, not a limitation**; §1–§1H **stay as written, explicitly not reissued**, historically accurate for what was checked at the time. §1B.5's "fourth argument for the register" records that its own missed edge is now `BE-SSC-014`, whose `consumed_by` names the WTC. §3.6 restated to "every load-bearing figure still outside the register."

